  "_notes": [
    "⚠ THE COMMIT LEG IS BROKEN — issue 858, found by this capture: the agent accepts the diff and the plant does not move. `commitAttempt` records that rather than pretending otherwise. Re-capture when 858 lands.",
    "\uD83D\uDEA9 lineDiffs[].fromGross / toGross are the ENGINE's gross — RepricingItemDiff's Old/NewGrossValue, which are PRE-DISCOUNT and EX-VAT. That is NOT the same number as the line's own lineTotal.gross, which is VAT-inclusive. RepricingItemDiff exposes no VAT-inclusive pair, and 804 carried the engine's value rather than computing one because the preview is what the confirm token PINS: a computed number would pin a figure the engine never produced. (857 divergence 2 — settled at capture.)",
    "promotionsMoved is EMPTY and will stay so until the engine's rebind diff reports per OFFER rather than per LINE (857 divergence 3).",
    "atpReFreeze carries fromQty/toQty NULL: no caller-supplied ATP map goes into the rebind (a fresh read is a remote hop per line and 287 says unknown ATP gates nothing), so 'availability not re-checked' is the true answer.",
    "The preview is run and NOT persisted — which is exactly why 129 needed no dryRun flag (§5.1). header.plant on the preview is still the OLD plant; only the commit moves it.",
    "The same requestId rides preview and commit."
  ]
}
